Import "General-chemistry.lingua"

General chemistry sources — books, courses, data, and research (@gc-sources: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @general-chemistry) { r_37CHT3QSMD33JDMXE59S6M2ME3
Use substantial books, complete course material, original explanatory Records, and precise primary references. Technical media stay at authorized external locations. The source Records distinguish open licences, conditional/free reading, current notices, and automated-access limits. No textbooks, PDFs, videos, simulations, datasets, or source collections are bundled.

**First and second readings:** [Chemistry 2e — Flowers, Theopold, Langley, and Robinson](sources/Chemistry-OpenStax.lingua#r_02Y5N2VMTTPBDSNYPD4Z26EZ94), [Chem1 General Chemistry Virtual Textbook — Stephen Lower](sources/Chem1-Lower.lingua#r_0NFQA43WZVMECZY6SKZJMRXWBZ), and [Química Geral I — Feitosa, Barbosa, and Forte](sources/Quimica-Geral-I-UECE.lingua#r_7N9JXVMC5DWB8P3MX79YYPHNPA) supply the whole introductory programme. [Principles of Chemical Science — MIT 5.111SC, Fall 2014](sources/MIT-5-111SC.lingua#r_312Z44VT67CCX60KG27PWM6NZ8) supplies a complete course with questions/problems/exams; [Principles of Chemical Science — MIT 5.112, Fall 2005](sources/MIT-5-112.lingua#r_05VDAXGTY0M9E5K9TMJTWTFNAG) supplies a stronger later lecture progression with stated preparation and a separately acquired commercial reading list. The latter's unavailable campus assessments are not represented as published resources.

**Practical work and measurement:** [Química geral no laboratório — Marcela Boroski, organizer](sources/Quimica-geral-no-laboratorio.lingua#r_48YEN2SA34DW0FPCSTMVTW3CTD), [Safety in Academic Chemistry Laboratories — ACS, eighth edition](sources/ACS-Academic-Laboratories.lingua#r_1GAGRBYCJGJAY86HQCNE9S66EP), [Laboratory Safety for Chemistry Students — Hill and Finster, third edition](sources/ACS-Laboratory-Safety-Textbook.lingua#r_7TD6AG2TZZ0GS0EWJMC8KC9SB0), [Prudent Practices in the Laboratory — National Research Council](sources/Prudent-Practices.lingua#r_3RPEFRP5NBW53ECS7EFQX6D6ZK), and the assigned complete chapters of [Analytical Chemistry 2.1 — David Harvey](sources/Analytical-Chemistry-Harvey.lingua#r_0XMY75E3FRXRGR3BK28V3JAC0T) connect theory with observation, practical competence, methods, and evidence. Registered/free platform access is identified separately from an open redistribution licence. [Measurement and metrology](../../inquiry/metrology/Metrology.lingua#r_3G54ENPA974K19AB5XF0P641N5), [The Fitness for Purpose of Analytical Methods — Eurachem](../../inquiry/metrology/sources/Method-Validation.lingua#r_5XXJY86AVZZ7XRT71EY7TRYDJY), [Quantifying Uncertainty in Analytical Measurement — Eurachem/CITAC](../../inquiry/metrology/sources/Analytical-Uncertainty.lingua#r_41N1P8BNZH26X9679RHB0THQNS), and [Worked measurement examples — JCGM GUM-5:2026](../../inquiry/metrology/sources/GUM-Examples-2026.lingua#r_4FVN1GYTH9X8M1JFWFNT696GR0) reuse existing general measurement sources and chemical examples.

**Definitions and evaluated data:** [Quantities, Units and Symbols in Physical Chemistry — IUPAC Green Book](sources/IUPAC-Green-Book.lingua#r_5SR8CP04E580VSV69MYQNSZ73F), [Nomenclature of Inorganic Chemistry — IUPAC Red Book and brief guide](sources/IUPAC-Red-Book.lingua#r_0CW26ZVGP8AR7QH2KXCM36MB4J), [Atomic weights, isotopes, and the periodic table — CIAAW and IUPAC](sources/Atomic-Weights-and-Isotopes.lingua#r_1HF97SGP3GF6YJDRH0D81PQ3S3), [NIST Chemistry WebBook — evaluated properties and their sources](sources/NIST-Chemistry-WebBook.lingua#r_7MMJR7YZKCS02QYACZM15GFQVP), [NIST-JANAF Thermochemical Tables — fourth-edition reference data](sources/NIST-JANAF.lingua#r_64N7R6GQB5B7NVW5KBXB3NYD44), and [Compilation of Henry’s law constants, version 5.0.0 — Rolf Sander](sources/Henry-Law-Sander.lingua#r_4HW63C2ZE42PFRFC294FDPTYWH). Record actual edition, convention, phase, temperature, units, source/evaluation, and uncertainty. A current download page can coexist with an older table edition. Read precise data and original references for a focused study; these are not instructions to mirror a database.

**Applications and optional virtual study:** [Mineral Commodity Summaries 2026 and silicon information — USGS](sources/Mineral-Commodities-USGS.lingua#r_1MSRN5WRD5DQT6Y6B7SDYZ8KWW) supplies a dated material/supply context; [Chemical models and interactive experiments — PhET, University of Colorado](sources/PhET-Chemistry.lingua#r_15P1XV6BQDZJM260GWM3VXHN6J) and [Virtual laboratory and quantitative exercises — ChemCollective](sources/ChemCollective-Virtual-Lab.lingua#r_246CB9EYQ2A1SQFHPV15F4Q4WT) offer optional external models whose assumptions and actual version/access need inspection. A simulation does not demonstrate practical laboratory competence. [Reproducible computational work](../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/Reproducible-computation.lingua#r_78FWWJDCV0ZGG7VYSPRCWN56DQ) provides the shared reproducible-computing foundation used by the original equilibrium example and research projects.

Assignments identify whole books, full chapters, course sequences, and exact later methods. Preserve actual component notices before retention or reuse. Metadata/access were checked on 29 October 2026 where reachable; the UECE naming/licence discrepancy, data-edition differences, registered-platform access, and untested interactive behavior remain explicit in the source descriptions.

